summary: |-
  Builder shipped phase A of T-2026-10-20-005 in commits 6ca8f0a3, f06ac152 and f55af625 on its worktree branch.
  - Voice client: a per-segment capture state machine with a closed drop-reason set; throttled ≤5 Hz, terminal states always sent.
  - Kernel: relays it as status.voice.capture with a 5 s TTL, voice principal only; the gui-only seam for V2 is built.
  - Level: the Swift level is finally consumed, so the meter shows real dBFS instead of a decorative CSS loop.
  - GUI: polls 1 s at rest and 175 ms while hearing; the polls now clear on disconnect (Aegis L2); lastError is sanitized (Aegis L1); the dead voice.turn.partial paths are removed.
  - Ids unchanged.
  - Suites: voice 102, gnomon 2247, gui 234, contracts 453.
  - Choices to check: a STT exception maps to no-words; echo is checked before too-short; possibly a double aria-live.
  Aegis review launched. Phase B (live words) is next, after the B0 benchmark.
